KORTEX PAST EXAMINATION PAPERS
MEDICINE - Human Anatomy (Year 2024)

Q1. Which cranial nerve provides parasympathetic innervation to abdominal viscera?
  (A) CN VII (Facial)
  (B) CN IX (Glossopharyngeal)
  (C) CN X (Vagus)
  (D) CN XII (Hypoglossal)
  Answer: C - The Vagus nerve (CN X) provides parasympathetic supply to thoracic and abdominal organs.


